    "explanation": "Finding on the core fact. Both advocates are right about the measurement, and the deviation is established. The GPS trace for TRP-03102 (EV-GPS-03102, weight 1.0) covers 100.0% of the trip with 113 fixes at a 10-second interval, an empty gaps array and max_gap_sec 0.0, so it is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) and no independent corroboration or POL-RD-10(3) escalation arises. It measures 14.37 km between the recorded pickup (06:30:55) and the recorded drop-off (06:49:35), against the booking-time optimal of 11.0 km on the trip record (EV-TRIP-03102, weight 1.0). Excess = 3.37 km = 30.64% of optimal, which clears both POL-RD-01 gates (greater than 20% and greater than 0.8 km). As POL-RD-01 requires, the governing figure is the trace's 14.37 km; the trip record's 14.4 km is a rounded convenience copy and was not used for the threshold test. The rider's claims on the measurement and on trace integrity are accepted, and the driver's concessions of the same points are accepted as far as they go. The driver's claim repeating that no POL-RD-10 trigger fires was discarded at the mechanical stage for not naming the advisory's issue code; the rider's independent claim to the same effect survives and is what I rely on. Not material. 30.64% is below the 50% limb and 3.37 km is below the 8.0 km limb, so this is not a MATERIAL deviation. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is therefore not required, and it would not help in any event: driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 231, below both POL-RD-06 triggers. There is no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c). I have not used the driver's lifetime counter prior_deviation_flags or the driver's rating: under POL-GEN-01 both are context only. The driver's traffic explanation. 'Traffic was heavy so I took another road' does not reduce the excess. The only traffic advisory for this trip, EV-ADVIS-03102-01, is MISSING - no payload, weight_multiplier 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - so POL-RD-03 cannot be run (no named segment the optimal route traverses, no validity window, no leave-and-rejoin check), and under POL-RD-08 and POL-RD-13 the assertion carries no weight, reduces no distance and supplies no amended optimal. Because no advisory identifier was cited in support of an exculpatory clause, POL-RD-13(1) applies and this is not an escalation under POL-RD-10(5). I record that the driver's traffic explanation is discarded as evidence and that no advisory was on file. The remaining exculpatory routes are equally unavailable, and both advocates agree: POL-RD-04 cannot be invoked because the chat log EV-CHAT-03102 holds 0 messages, so there is no rider instruction, no timestamp and no waypoint_hint to corroborate; POL-RD-05 cannot be run because no pickup or dropoff amendment is recorded and amended_optimal_distance_km is null; POL-RD-12 does not apply because the vehicle type is RYDE_X, not RYDE_POOL, and solo_optimal_distance_km is null; POL-RD-11 does not apply because the fare model is METERED and quoted_fare_sgd is null, so the rider's 'quoted' framing buys no fixed-price remedy and the distance-and-time refund route stays open. The remedy is arithmetic under POL-RD-02, read off the fare breakdown EV-FARE-03102 (weight 1.0), with the surge multiplier read from fare_breakdown.surge_multiplier = 1.0, on the booked optimal route: charged_total = SGD 20.64; recomputed_fare = (3.80 + 0.75 x 11.0 + 0.28 x 14.9) x 1.0, plus 0.80 platform fee, plus 0.00 ERP and tolls, plus 0.00 waiting_time_fee, minus 0.00 promo_discount = SGD 17.0220; refund = 20.64 - 17.0220 = 3.6180, rounded UP to SGD 3.65. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis threshold and is 17.5% of charged_total, far below the 90% share that would substitute a full refund, so the outcome is a PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 3.65. The rider put SGD 3.00 in issue on the dispute record; the refund is fixed by the fare arithmetic and SGD 3.65 is the payable figure the fare breakdown enumerates, so SGD 3.65 is what is returned. Nothing is added on top under POL-RD-09: erp_gantries is empty, tolls/ERP are 0.00, the airport surcharge is 0.00 on a trip that did not originate at an airport, waiting_time_fee is 0.00 and promo_discount is 0.00, so there is no pass-through correction, no phantom gantry and no billing-integrity referral. No driver compensation is due: POL-RD-04's compensation limb requires the fare breakdown to bill less distance than the trace records, and here the billed distance (14.4 km) matches the trace (14.37 km), so there is no unbilled shortfall. NO_ACTION is not the outcome: on this rider-filed dispute it would leave the whole SGD 20.64 with the rider, payment_status being CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0. The POL-RD-08 rider-profile proviso did not bite: deviation_claims_60d is 1, below the 4-or-more trigger, with 0 substantiated, and in any case the excess is at the 30% line on an unimpaired trace. Confidence. The deciding facts - the trace distance, the optimal distance and the fare arithmetic - are carried by EV-GPS-03102, EV-TRIP-03102 and EV-FARE-03102, each at weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and this ruling is well clear of the 0.70 floor in POL-RD-10(1). Confidence is 0.90. The monetary effect, SGD 3.65, is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold in POL-GEN-05, so it executes on issue. This is a provisional ruling; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
